er-events_catalog":"2017-02-03","stage19_causal_queue":"2017-02-03","stage21_crosswalk":"2017-02-03"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:13772","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Section 1. Policy. It shall be the policy of my Administration to regulate \nthe United States financial system in a manner consistent with the following \nprinciples of regulation, which shall be known as the Core Principles:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1 (lead-in)","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) empower Americans to make independent financial decisions and in-\nformed choices in the marketplace, save for retirement, and build individual \nwealth;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) prevent taxpayer-funded bailouts;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) foster economic growth and vibrant financial markets through more \nrigorous regulatory impact analysis that addresses systemic risk and market \nfailures, such as moral hazard and information asymmetry;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) enable American companies to be competitive with foreign firms in \ndomestic and foreign markets;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(d)","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec1(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) advance American interests in international financial regulatory negotia-\ntions and meetings;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(e)","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec1(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(f) make regulation efficient, effective, and appropriately tailored; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(f)","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec1(f)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(g) restore public accountability within Federal financial regulatory agen-\ncies and rationalize the Federal financial regulatory framework.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1(g)","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec1(g)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Directive to the Secretary of the Treasury. The Secretary of the \nTreasury shall consult with the heads of the member agencies of the Financial \nStability Oversight Council and shall report to the President within 120 \ndays of the date of this order (and periodically thereafter) on the extent \nto which existing laws, treaties, regulations, guidance, reporting and record-\nkeeping requirements, and other Government policies promote the Core Prin-\nciples and what actions have been taken, and are currently being taken, \nto promote and support the Core Principles. That report, and all subsequent \nreports, shall identify any laws, treaties, regulations, guidance, reporting \nand recordkeeping requirements, and other Government policies that inhibit \nFederal regulation of the United States financial system in a manner con-\nsistent with the Core Principles.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"82 FR 9965, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2","sha256":"9d06883ab5a4e45f112b1df02c3d9765d5f0273de6db2454b9a2ef2e368dedee","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2017-02-08/pdf/2017-02762.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13772#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Nothing in this order shall be construed \nto impair or otherwise affect: \n(i) the authority granted by law to an executive department or agency, \nor the head thereof; or \n(ii) the functions of the Director of the Office of Management and Budget \nrelating to budgetary, administrative, or legislative proposals.","original_source":{"pag